NEMU (6502EMU)
==============

This directory is a fork of NEMU (NJU Emulator), originally developed by the
NJU-ProjectN team:

    https://github.com/NJU-ProjectN/nemu

NEMU is licensed under the Mulan Permissive Software License, Version 2
(Mulan PSL v2). The complete license text is in LICENSE next to this file.
You may obtain a copy of Mulan PSL v2 at:

    http://license.coscl.org.cn/MulanPSL2

The MOS 6502/65C02 ISA port, the NES/Famicom frontend (PPU, APU, controller,
iNES mappers), the 6502EMU launcher and the demo ROM builder in this tree were
written for Open6502 and are released under the same license.

Redistribution, in source or binary form, must include a copy of the Mulan
PSL v2 text and retain the copyright and disclaimer statements of the
components below.

Third-party components inside this tree
---------------------------------------

  tools/kconfig/          Linux kernel kconfig, GPL-2.0.
                          Build-time only: compiles the `conf` tool. The tool
                          is not linked into the emulator.

  tools/qemu-diff/        GDB remote protocol client, Copyright (C) 2015
                          Red Hat Inc., GPL-3.0-or-later. Development-only
                          difftest helper; not built by default.

  src/device/mmc.h        Copyright 2002 Hewlett-Packard Company. "Use
                          consistent with the GNU GPL is permitted, provided
                          that this copyright notice is preserved in its
                          entirety in all copies and derived works."

  basic/                  Microsoft BASIC 1.1 disassembly (KIM-1 build) from
                          Michael Steil's msbasic project, BSD-2-Clause.
                          See basic/README.md for the full text.

  nesgame/                Open6502 demo game, MIT (part of Open6502).

Runtime dependencies are resolved from the system and are not redistributed
here: SDL2 (zlib) when built with the SDL frontend, and libedit (BSD) or GNU
readline (GPL-3.0) for the interactive monitor.
